# ShellCheck configuration for the whole pack.
#
# CI (.github/workflows/verify.yml) runs, from the repository root:
#     shellcheck -x $(git ls-files '*.sh')
# and fails on anything not disabled here. Reproduce locally with that exact command - ShellCheck
# only picks this file up when it is invoked from the pack root.
#
# CI pins ShellCheck to the version below rather than using the runner's apt package. They disagree:
# 0.9.0 (apt, Ubuntu 24.04) still reports checks 0.11.0 has dropped - it failed CI on SC2002, which
# 0.11.0 does not emit - so an unpinned gate would break for a reason you cannot reproduce locally.
# Use 0.11.0 to match CI.
#
# The gate is pinned at ZERO errors and ZERO warnings (baseline measured 2026-10-14, ShellCheck
# 0.11.0: 0 errors, 0 warnings, 36 notes). Each note category is disabled deliberately:
#
#   SC2015 (26)  `A && B || C` in tests/run.sh, tests/invariants.sh and one install.sh line. B is
#                always a deliberate `ok "..."`/`say "..."` and C its `bad "..."` fallback, so C
#                runs only if B itself failed (a printf error), never because A failed. Neither
#                suite sets `-e`, and rewriting 26 harness assertions as if/then would churn the
#                code that verifies everything else in the pack for no behavioural change.
#   SC2181 (4)   `[ $? -eq 0 ]` in the suites: the exit code is captured on purpose so it can be
#                reported with its own PASS/FAIL line naming the expected code.
#   SC2295 (3)   Unquoted ${x} nested inside ${..} in a test-harness pattern match.
#   SC2012 (2)   `ls` rather than `find` in the suites, over pack-controlled filenames.
#   SC1003 (1)   An escaped single quote inside a grep pattern in tests/invariants.sh.
#
# Every one of these is in the test harnesses except a single SC2015 in install.sh. A finding in a
# new file - or any new warning anywhere - still fails CI.
disable=SC2015,SC2181,SC2295,SC2012,SC1003
